  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Support through NFIs and Shelter for IDPs Affected by Cyclone Gamane in Northern Madagascar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tropical Cyclone Gamane made landfall on 27 March 2024 in the commune of Ampisikinana, Voh&#xe9;mar district, Sava region, in the North of Madagascar. The cyclone caused heavy rains and floods, leaving a total of 19 dead, 4 missing and more than 22,000 evacuees/displaced people, including 2,714 pregnant women. Tropical Cyclone Gamane caused massive damage, with nearly 5,000 houses destroyed and 199 partially destroyed; over 18,000 houses and several thousand hectares of rice fields flooded; traditional houses made of earth and flooded at the verge of collapse at any moment; 101 schools flooded; and 22 health facilities partially damaged. Through this Central Emergency Response Fund Rapid Response allocation, the International Organization for Migration is responding to the urgent needs of populations affected by Tropical Cyclone Gamane through the provision of in-kind and cash for non-food items, as well as the rehabilitation of damaged and destroyed shelters.</narrative>
  </description>
